        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Home Depot carries everything you need to seal a driveway well, but the aisle rewards shoppers who arrive knowing their surface and their square footage. For blacktop, Latex-ite Airport Grade is the safe all-round choice, BLACK JACK Drive-Maxx 1000 is the premium step up, and Rust-Oleum EpoxyShield Blacktop is the value pick. For concrete, choose Foundation Armor SX5000 for invisible protection or BEHR Wet-Look for shine.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, buy a spare pail, spend as much time on prep as on sealing, and wait for a proper weather window. The pail is the easy part; the weekend you put into the driveway is what decides how long it lasts.
          </p>
